 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Inference Search:** Inference requires finding the correct model for a query point, which is a search problem. Spatial hashing is used to accelerate this [S1].
-*   **Boundary Artifacts:** Without ghost cells, adjacent networks trained independently may produce discontinuous outputs at interfaces [S1, see Subtopics].
-*   **Sparse Data:** Regions with sparse data may converge quickly, allowing for early stopping (down to 20 seconds per model) [S1].
+*   **Inference Search:** Inference requires finding the correct model for a query point, which is a search problem mitigated by spatial hashing [S1].
+*   **Sparse Data:** Regions with sparse data may converge quickly, allowing early stopping (down to 20 seconds per model) [S1].
+*   **Ghost Cell Extents:** Pre-calculating network extents must explicitly include ghost cells when using the overlapping variant to ensure boundary continuity [S1].
 
